From 0be0da595bf849c6dac2d8e63fb1efc844acc3b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:14:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] feat(reframe): one layout for the whole clip instead of
 switching per shot

Luffy's first try-it clip (a handheld awards-night vlog) had been cut
into 40 shots in 58 s, each choosing fit or a face crop, so the picture
jumped between a zoomed crop and a small fit with blurred bands every
second or two. unify_layout_plan sums screen time per layout family
(fit / face-crop / split); a clip that mixes families is re-planned
with the winner (the always-fit plan or the always-crop face-tracked
plan). Split-dominant (two-person) and delegated facecam clips keep the
planner's plan. REFRAME_CONSISTENT=0 restores per-shot switching.

On that clip: fit 43.7 s vs crop 14.3 s, so the whole clip is fit.
The harness gains --framing auto|fit|crop and the try-it page a Layout
picker (Auto one-layout / face-follow crop / whole frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
